<section>
  <h2>Choose the wedding security duties you need</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card"><h3>Gate guards and darwan</h3><p>Venue entrance cover, invitation or guest-list checks agreed with the host, vendor entry coordination and guidance to the correct entrance.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Bouncers and crowd management</h3><p>Request bouncers for busy reception entrances, queues and controlled-access areas. The brief focuses on calm communication, de-escalation and coordination with the host and venue.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Guest and family access</h3><p>Identify agreed family-only rooms or backstage areas and manage entry according to the host's instructions. Discuss female security personnel if your event requires them; availability must be confirmed.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Vehicle-entry coordination</h3><p>Help direct vehicles within the venue's agreed parking and drop-off arrangements, keeping entrance routes clear with venue staff. Public-road arrangements must be handled with the relevant authorities.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Vendor and equipment access</h3><p>Agree an entry process for decorators, caterers, photographers and other vendors, including access during setup and pack-down if included in the booking.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Evening or overnight cover</h3><p>Request separate shifts when functions run late or the venue needs overnight guarding. Share finish times and handover requirements when requesting your quote.</p></div>
  </div>
  <p>Guards and bouncers provide the agreed security duties. Catering, decoration, wedding planning and valet driving are separate services and are not included in a security booking.</p>
</section>

