<section>
  <h2>Wedding security questions</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>Can I book guards or bouncers for just one day?</dt><dd>Yes, you can request one-day or short-term cover. Dates, duty hours, staff availability and the agreed scope must be confirmed before booking.</dd>
    <dt>Can the same team cover a wedding and reception over several days?</dt><dd>Ask for a plan covering each date and venue. Team continuity, rest periods and any replacement shifts are confirmed during scheduling.</dd>
    <dt>How many guards or bouncers should I request?</dt><dd>Share your guest count, venue layout, entrances, vehicle access and any restricted rooms. The team can propose staffing for those duties; guest count alone does not determine the requirement.</dd>
    <dt>Do I need a long-term contract?</dt><dd>You can enquire for a fixed wedding or function period rather than a monthly guarding arrangement. The written booking should state the exact dates and terms.</dd>
    <dt>Can I ask for wedding-season or last-minute availability?</dt><dd>Call or WhatsApp with your venue and dates. Availability must be checked; sending an enquiry is not a confirmed booking.</dd>
  </dl>
</section>

